lude the structure and function of the nervous system, physiological approaches to understanding behavior, hormones and behavior, biological bases of sensation and perception, learning and memory, cognition, emotion, and communication.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "May be used to satisfy Psychology major breadth requirement and as an alternative prerequisite for upper-level biopsychology courses.", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "HE", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2846, "crseId": 372168, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "HD", "catalogNbr": "2350", "titleShort": "Early Multilingualism", "titleLong": "Multilingualism and Multiculturalism in Early Childhood", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1626, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "06/20/2023", "endDt": "07/28/2023", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "yek2", "firstName": "Yarden", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Kedar"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": null, "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": null, "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "This Online Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=3461"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "06/20/2023", "endDt": "07/28/2023", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "AD", "instrModeDescrshort": "DL-AD", "instrModeDescr": "Distance Learning-Asynchronous", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRD", "gradingBasisShort": "Graded", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "PSYCH", "catalogNbr": "2350", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "6WK", "sessionBeginDt": "06/20/2023", "sessionEndDt": "08/01/2023", "sessionLong": "Six Week Summer", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "Children who grow up in multilingual environments have a profoundly different experience compared to monolingual children. In this course, we examine the nature and impact of this experience on the socio-emotional, cognitive, and linguistic development of young children, focusing on the complex multilingual and multicultural reality in Israel as our main case study. Specifically, we explore the multilingual development of children from several minority and immigrant groups in Israel: Arabs, Former Soviet Union (FSU) and Ethiopian immigrants, Israeli-born children of labor migrants, deaf communities, among others.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "Fall 2022 will be the final offerring of this course.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": ["Discuss the substance and validity of theories and empirical studies on first and second language acquisition.", "Discern and describe different developmental factors (i.e., linguistic, cognitive, and socio-emotional) that are affected by children's multilingual experience.", "Apply knowledge gained in objectives #1 & #2 to analyze and critique current developmental studies on the multilingual and multicultural experience of young children and adolescents in Israel."], "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "HE", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2846, "crseId": 351513, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "HD", "catalogNbr": "2600", "titleShort": "Intro to Personality", "titleLong": "Introduction to Personality", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1120, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "05/30/2023", "endDt": "06/16/2023", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 6, "netid": "vz29", "firstName": "Vivian", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Zayas"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDescrshort": "Online", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "This Online Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=1015"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "05/30/2023", "endDt": "06/16/2023", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "AD", "instrModeDescrshort": "DL-AD", "instrModeDescr": "Distance Learning-Asynchronous", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "PSYCH", "catalogNbr": "2750", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "3W1", "sessionBeginDt": "05/30/2023", "sessionEndDt": "06/16/2023", "sessionLong": "Three Week - First", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "What is \"personality\"? How is it scientifically studied and measured? To what extent, do biological, social, and cultural factors shape personality? Is personality an expression of our genetic make up and biology, the culmination of social influences, the interplay of both, or the result of random events? In this course, we will review the major theoretical paradigms of personality psychology, discuss contemporary research, theory, and methodology, and learn about key historical debates in the study of \"personality\".", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, Winter, Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: introductory psychology or human development course recommended.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "HE", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2846, "crseId": 351564, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "HD", "catalogNbr": "2810", "titleShort": "Intro To Social Psych", "titleLong": "Introduction to Social Psychology", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1158, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "08:30AM", "timeEnd": "11:30AM", "startDt": "05/30/2023", "endDt": "06/16/2023", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 6, "netid": "mn589", "firstName": "Minghui", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Ni"}], "pattern": "MTWRF", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDe